{"title":"2020 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2020 AMC 10B Problems\">2020 AMC 10B #3</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2020 AMC 12B Problems\">2020 AMC 12B #3</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(One_Sentence)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (One Sentence)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(HOW_TO_THINK_CREATIVELY!!!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (HOW TO THINK CREATIVELY!!!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solutions\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solutions</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The ratio of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/e/9ee4b825a2e36ae093ed7be5e4851ef453b34914.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/f/def7726c2babb527f7ab2ae4c436cc012ebbd351.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4:3$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"32\" height=\"13\" />, the ratio of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/e/80e47d95347d6e72d1b3e8a4aea3dd20082f3cc3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3:2$\" width=\"32\" height=\"12\" />, and the ratio of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/7/9272fbcdbe136e6528e3f6d3ded14eaead70d0ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1:6$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"32\" height=\"13\" />. What is the ratio of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/e/9ee4b825a2e36ae093ed7be5e4851ef453b34914.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/3/ee326c993c95f1656496d2d74ca2270dd268c4c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y?$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"17\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/8/8983c70c40b17d964f2592f83651f94301343734.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 4:3 \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 3:2 \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\  8:3 \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 4:1 \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 16:3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"479\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28One_Sentence.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(One_Sentence)\">Solution 1 (One Sentence)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (One Sentence)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/8/4580380e3bcdc9c7b1cabee62a47ff4ebdf74718.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac wy = \\frac wx \\cdot \\frac xz \\cdot \\frac zy = \\frac43\\cdot\\frac61\\cdot\\frac23=\\frac{16}{3},\\]\" width=\"251\" height=\"41\" /> from which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/d/b3d64561a8d93c210e17e41c3ba97166298106cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w:y=\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\ 16:3}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"152\" height=\"28\" />\n</p><p>~MRENTHUSIASM\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We need to somehow link all three of the ratios together. We can start by connecting the last two ratios together by multiplying the last ratio by two. \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/2/c42999a387ad89a76eb539c8df7440866d9d54df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z:x=1:6=2:12$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"158\" height=\"13\" />, and since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51d27dfd7eeb68d64cdd61d4fac2b2c2c32304be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y:z=3:2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"91\" height=\"16\" />, we can link them together to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/a/c6a8c6b85e55e379f108d8e9befc861434188e48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y:z:x=3:2:12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"149\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>Finally, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/3/e13e300cdc6149678cbc3ea2e6c45ff888a0f3e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x:w=3:4=12:16$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"171\" height=\"13\" />, we can link this again to get: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/2/142f7b4a7a4a6748e0390c90d21a23afa3434d15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y:z:x:w=3:2:12:16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"211\" height=\"16\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/7/c472cb9d3734ae8065f436dd1a229c9649fd95b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w:y = \\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\ 16:3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"149\" height=\"28\" />. \n</p><p>~quacker88\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We have the equations <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/3/8e326e61d7565edb30c87b18aca27e3d80a6d5e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{w}{x}=\\frac{4}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"53\" height=\"37\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/d/ceddfe824e2a38ffd5e0516bcfae35bb47393f56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{y}{z}=\\frac{3}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"49\" height=\"37\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/2/442a388338229bd490b60135d03568f8f827d328.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{z}{x}=\\frac{1}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"50\" height=\"37\" />.\nClearing denominators, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0614fd50df53125cd8a75fc3fb959b1b980bafca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3w = 4x$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"66\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/9/4e934419d73b3d0443b16397698429f9f74299f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2y = 3z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"60\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/c/b1c5a3b2e8aaf9595c2605e0a336d82f8c4376ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6z = x$\" width=\"52\" height=\"12\" />. \nSince we want <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/4/aa445bd621241d5c47b3ca6494db0812cf456355.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{w}{y}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"19\" height=\"38\" />, we look to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> in terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> since we know the relationship between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/e/9ee4b825a2e36ae093ed7be5e4851ef453b34914.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" />.\nWe begin by multiplying both sides of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/9/4e934419d73b3d0443b16397698429f9f74299f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2y = 3z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"60\" height=\"16\" /> by two, obtaining <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/5/0c51d5ee13821af4d17bd826596e4c53e0e9a21c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4y = 6z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"60\" height=\"16\" />. We then substitute that into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/c/b1c5a3b2e8aaf9595c2605e0a336d82f8c4376ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6z = x$\" width=\"52\" height=\"12\" /> \nto get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/2/52221b05aa42d226a79386ac2cce286233f34bcf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4y = x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"53\" height=\"15\" /> . Now, to be able to substitute this into out first equation, we need to have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/4/ed4977828049d99f20ccd3b4acb6bbd43c2eb70f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4x$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" /> on the RHS. \nMultiplying both sides by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/4/1c4ae3c155396f0f565501921676dacb01a26c91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16y = 4x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"71\" height=\"16\" />. \nSubstituting this into our first equation, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/2/c42796b59d8c360f27fb1c653c4769a6c8177802.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3w = 16y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"74\" height=\"16\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/d/34d0b42de8320db74523391ebf9ba08696902bd6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{w}{y}=\\frac{16}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"62\" height=\"41\" />, so our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/1/321ce0708d0cb6af1ba0b726d06babc9ed9686c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\ 16:3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"87\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>~Binderclips1\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>WLOG, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/8/a980f1d003784beac1ff133070f45f23401bf89f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"49\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/2/b022dc8ef6d33931fc1ae3d27df3ea0a81b52936.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>Since the ratio of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/7/9272fbcdbe136e6528e3f6d3ded14eaead70d0ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1:6$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"32\" height=\"13\" />, we can substitute in the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/b/e2bc701f5e6cda908832d291fff917d06129f012.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{z}{3}=\\frac{1}{6} \\implies z=\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"145\" height=\"37\" />. \n</p><p>The ratio of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/e/80e47d95347d6e72d1b3e8a4aea3dd20082f3cc3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3:2$\" width=\"32\" height=\"12\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/3/bc3354f939aeb41c0c672bef6edab2ac7a891b0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{y}{\\frac{1}{2}}=\\frac{3}{2} \\implies y=\\frac{3}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"146\" height=\"44\" />. \n</p><p>The ratio of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/e/9ee4b825a2e36ae093ed7be5e4851ef453b34914.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/3/a93e3bf35ac4def72a19a3343dbf10e873552e31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4}{\\frac{3}{4}}=\\frac{16}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"63\" height=\"45\" /> so our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/1/321ce0708d0cb6af1ba0b726d06babc9ed9686c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\ 16:3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"87\" height=\"28\" />. \n</p><p>~quacker88\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/5/a65aa11fadd02fc371dc65a887041c316a1e3edd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{w}{x}=\\frac{4}{3}, \\frac{y}{z}=\\frac{3}{2}, \\frac{z}{x}=\\frac{1}{6}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"180\" height=\"38\" /> Find LCD: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/d/d8d47558946807a0a907d53bf062dfbbf9784ae1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{w}{x}=\\frac{8}{6}, \\frac{z}{x}=\\frac{1}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"116\" height=\"38\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/7/a576c89b5ca3fc192c1742c3bf44e1dcc490b726.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{w}{z}=\\frac{8}{1}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"62\" height=\"38\" /> Similarly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/2/5924d7699d4d797117d40cd7fcaad5079d0c667e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{w}{z}=\\frac{16}{2}, \\frac{y}{z}=\\frac{3}{2},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"130\" height=\"38\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/b/90baf3c1c052080311e4401f977c75b633925025.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{w}{y}=\\frac{16}{3},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"71\" height=\"42\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/1/321ce0708d0cb6af1ba0b726d06babc9ed9686c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\ 16:3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"87\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>~Yelechi\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28HOW_TO_THINK_CREATIVELY.21.21.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(HOW_TO_THINK_CREATIVELY!!!)\">Video Solution (HOW TO THINK CREATIVELY!!!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (HOW TO THINK CREATIVELY!!!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QqkNnsNEgiA\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QqkNnsNEgiA</a> (for AMC 10)\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/Lz6XmHr8tJE\">https://youtu.be/Lz6XmHr8tJE</a> (for AMC 12)\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solutions\">Video Solutions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solutions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/Gkm5rU5MlOU\">https://youtu.be/Gkm5rU5MlOU</a> (for AMC 10)\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/WfTty8Fe5Fo\">https://youtu.be/WfTty8Fe5Fo</a> (for AMC 12)\n</p><p><br />\n<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/y4BbRapJepY\">https://youtu.be/y4BbRapJepY</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/wH7xhYxwaFc\">https://youtu.be/wH7xhYxwaFc</a>\n</p><p>~AlexExplains\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/